  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A selection of two open part edges is now a band for the pocket family (2D Offset, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive). Before, the selection was refused with \"... is an open run - a 2D Offset cannot end mid-edge ...\".\n- The definition of the region is exact (`crates/app/src/operation/open_band.rs`, new):\n  - Picked open runs that share an end are welded into one wall. Exactly two walls, A and B, must remain. Each wall is level. The two walls are at one height.\n  - Each wall is run on straight along the tangent at each end.\n  - S is the stock outline in XY, grown by the extension `e` with sharp corners.\n  - `band(e) = (side of A that holds B) ∩ (side of B that holds A) ∩ S`.\n- `band(0)` is the region of the selection. The pocket region law then removes the standing material of the part at each cut plane, as it does for a closed pick.\n- `band(e)` is a lane. `boundary::resolve` clips the area to the lane after the extension step. Thus \"Extend past\" moves the open ends out of the stock along the edges. The extension does not make the band wider, and the tool does not go round the end of a wall.\n- A selection with no clear band is refused by name:\n  - no stock in the setup;\n  - a wall that is not level, or walls at different heights;\n  - walls at more than 45 degrees to each other, or walls that do not run alongside each other;\n  - walls that cross or touch when run on, or that run together inside the stock;\n  - a stock outline that does not cover the space between the walls, or that closes the band in more than one piece;\n  - more than two walls, three edges at one point, open edges mixed with closed boundaries, an open edge of the stock;\n  - tool containment On or Outside.\n- One open edge keeps the old refusal, word for word. A tilted tool plane keeps the old refusal.\n- No gouge check or collision check is changed. The band operation answers to the same section law and to the solid law against the other parts of the setup.\n- The hooks are small: one call in `selection_geometry_in` (`selection.rs`), one clip in `boundary::resolve`, one field in `AreaCtx`. `stitch::gather_runs` is now `pub(super)`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1735-open-edge-band.md` (the definition and the options dropped).\n- No new command, thus no new MCP tool.\n\n## Readings\n\nFixture: a 40 x 40 x 20 block with a 16 mm slot (|x| <= 8) down to Z 10, in a 70 x 70 stock, 10 mm tool. The readings are the same for the three kinds.\n\n- Extension 0: the tool centre stays in |x| <= 3 and goes to y = ±30 (the tool edge is at the stock edge). 0 warnings.\n- Extension 7: the tool centre goes to y = ±37 and stays in |x| <= 3. 0 warnings.\n- Bottom at Z 5 (below the slot floor): cuts occur only at |y| >= 25, outside the part.\n- A second part (\"clamp\") in the open end of the band: the operation has `Warning::Gouge` findings, and the post is refused with \"post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 156 cell(s)\". No file is written.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests in `crates/app/tests/open_band.rs`:\n- `two_open_slot_edges_cut_the_band_up_to_the_stock_edge`\n- `the_extension_moves_the_open_ends_out_of_the_stock_along_the_walls`\n- `a_bottom_under_the_slot_floor_never_cuts_the_part`\n- `a_selection_with_no_clear_band_is_refused_by_name`\n- `with_no_stock_nothing_closes_the_band`\n- `the_selection_account_names_the_band`\n- `a_band_pass_that_cuts_another_part_blocks_the_post` (expects the refusal)\n\nUnit tests in `crates/app/src/operation/open_band_tests.rs`:\n- `the_band_is_the_strip_between_the_walls_closed_by_the_stock`\n- `unclear_walls_are_refused_by_name`\n- `runs_that_share_an_end_weld_into_one_wall`\n\nThe unit test found one defect during the work: two walls on one line gave half of the stock as the band. A touch check now refuses that selection, and the test pins it.\n\nGate (Windows): \n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on commit c18717ddf: app suites ok (1509 s, the lib tests and 190 suites, because the gate map names `app::operation`), ui suites ok (141 s), 0 failed.\n- The head commit 106ceb692 changes only `open_band.rs` for clippy (explicit NaN tests, a type alias). After it: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean, `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test open_band` passes (7 tests), and the 3 unit tests pass. The full quick gate was not run again on the head commit.\n\nNo golden file and no snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real model `Block-w-slot.step`. It is not a tracked file. The tests use a synthetic slotted block.\n- The GUI. No test clicks the two edges in the viewport.\n- Curved walls and walls of a STEP tessellation. The fixture walls are straight.\n- A tilted setup and turned stock.\n- Linux and macOS, the batch tier and the release tier.\n- A merge with draft PR #1756 (issue 1727, the open boundary path). `git merge-tree` of this head with head 52e4c70c gives no conflict. The merged tree was not built.\n\n## Limits\n\n- With extension 0 the tool centre stops one tool radius inside the stock edge. An extension of one tool radius or more clears the stock edge.\n- A blind slot picked as one U-shaped run stays refused as one open run. Follow-up: #1762.\n- Walls that meet inside the stock (a wedge with one open end) are refused by name. Follow-up: #1763.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Offset, 2D Pocket or 2D Adaptive with two opposite open edges selected now cuts the band between the edges up to the stock edge, and the extension moves the open ends out of the stock along the edges; an unclear selection is refused by name.\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1735\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
